From a17294f5c8e6359d77b666a9686534fb3a1bda91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 17:46:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 29/52] kaiair: LDP no longer feeds back into power control
 (align with LDP-TR)

The paper's direction is p -> X: power control holds the per-transmission
reliability p (PktR beta), and LDP derives the required transmission
opportunities X = ceil(log_{1-p}(1-P)) from p and the packet target P,
reserving them before the deadline. An earlier revision inverted this
(deadline -> N(D) -> relaxed per-tx requirement fed into the Cantelli
cushion); that departed from the paper and was also the mechanism behind
the LDP-ON cushion collapse. Removed:
- ldp_effective_tx_beta deleted; ldp_required_tx_count (paper Eq.) added
- UL cushion, DL BLER target and DL SINR-mode k now use the static beta
- feedback view prints N(D) vs X_required with a schedulability verdict
- unit tests updated (7/7 kaiair suites pass)
Scheduler-side LDP (deadline abandonment, N(D) retx cap, urgency ordering)
is unchanged, that is the paper's actual mechanism.
